    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1101">

                <pb facs="1074" n="908" xml:id="pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/20493</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Funston to the
                            Adjutant General
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Sam Houston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4447. Reference your number 5767, General Pershing makes following report: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Twenty-one Mexican prisoners have been sent to Columbus, New Mexico and
                            are held in stockade there. They can be securely held there for any
                            length of time pending decision by the State Department. Total number
                            these prisoners 21, all of whom are alleged to have been connected with
                            Columbus, New Mexico, raid.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Funston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
